  "result": "I found no matching ticket in the archive.\n\n{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket in the archive that reports this problem. The nearest tickets (#4560 and #3178) are about the Settings UI not saving the filename format. They are a different problem and were fixed in 2020. Your analysis looks sound, so I'd treat this as a new bug. The cause is that `Settings.Reload()` saves the defaults when `settings.json` is missing, and serializing `FileNameFormat` caches `_fileNameFormat` from the default `FileName`. The `FileName` setter never clears that cache. The fix you suggest is to clear `_fileNameFormat` in the `FileName` setter and mark `FileNameFormat` as `[JsonIgnore]`. Until that lands, run the CLI once so `settings.json` is created, or open Image Resizer settings once, and then your `--filename` value will be used.\"}",
